    "updated_at": "2016-01-11T17:36:20Z",
    "body": "So, another way of viewing this is that the HTML Standard redefines what these DTD public identifiers mean and that their original definition is now moot/obsolete. That seems to be the interpretation of implementations. However, I personally don't see much of a problem adding one identifier that is less tainted by legacy.\n",
